title: Staal's Schemes
subtitle: Chancellor Staal claims to have a plan to save the Commonwealth...
view-if: year >= 1932 and president = "DuFour" and chancellor = "Staal" and marcher_in_government = 0 and largest_party = "Royalist" and gallax_deported = 0 and not presidential_powers
on-arrival: economic_growth += 1; budget -= 1; disfavored -= 3 if disfavored > 10; landed_traditionalist += 3; guild_traditionalist += 3; burgher_traditionalist += 3; commons_traditionalist += 3
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/portraits/SchleicherKurt.jpg
#tags: event

= Staal's Schemes

Chancellor Kurt von Staal claims to have a plan to save the Commonwealth, and he has reached out to the Social Democrats with vague promises. He claims that in order to govern, the Assembly must be temporarily suspended to prevent the Royalists and Communists from disrupting government, in effect giving him and DuFour dictatorial powers. In the meantime, he is enacting a public works program and job creation plan, which he claims will stabilize the economy, 

[? if works_program <= 0: The trade unions are somewhat favorable to Staal's plan, as they see a commonality between Staal's economic plan and the ADGB's WTB-plan for debt-funded job creation. However, the rest of our party is vehemently against Staal. ?]

Rumors are that Staal is also reaching out to the Royalists with similar promises of cooperation; he seems to believe that he can "tame" the Royalists. Most in our party do not trust him to not bring the Royalists to power. In addition, working with him would essentially mean the end of our claim to be a "democratic" party.

# if this works: delay elections by 1 year (requires over 50% support - need Z and Golds and others to join as well based on relations; Traditionalists might support? Also should depend on DuFour relations).


- @accept
- @reject

@accept
title: Accept Staal's schemes.
subtitle: We will support the suspension of the Assembly.

Are we sure that we wish to do this? The vast majority of the party is against this proposal.

- @accept_2
- @reject

@accept_2
title: Accept Staal's schemes.
subtitle: We will support the suspension of the Assembly.
on-arrival: staal_support = marcher_r; commons_marcher -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 3; reformist_dissent += 20; left_dissent += 30; center_dissent += 30; knight_dissent += 25; pro_republic -= 10; staal_support += unionist_r if unionist_relation >= 50; staal_support += other_r + gold_r if gold_relation >= 30; staal_support += traditionalist_r if collectivist_relation <= 10 and left_strength + center_strength < labor_strength; labor_dissent -= 10
go-to: schleicher_success if staal_support >= 50; schleicher_failed if staal_support < 50

# There isn't enough resolution in this game to create conditions for when the Traditionalists would support Staal. It's possible that Marchers support for Staal would push Mallin to ally with Gallax.

With the exception of the trade unions, every faction of the Marchers is horrified by this betrayal of democracy.

[? if collectivist_relation <= 10 and left_strength + center_strength < labor_strength: Somehow, the Traditionalists has agreed to Staal's proposal, forming a temporary alliance with the general against Royalists and Communists. ?][? if unionist_relation >= 50 : The Unionist Party also supports Staal's plan. ?][? if gold_relation >= 30 : In addition, the Golds and some other smaller parties support this proposal. ?][? if collectivist_relation > 10 or left_strength + center_strength >= labor_strength: The Traditionalists, despite being courted by Staal, is not interested in joining this alliance. Traditionalists chairman Mallin seems to prefer working with Gallax to any alliance that includes the SPD. ?]

@schleicher_success
on-arrival: time_to_election = 13; schleichers_scheme_success = 1; next_election_time = 10000;
call: set_next_election_time

# hack to set next election time

The scheme has succeeded - there is a majority in the Assembly backing Staal. New elections have been tentatively set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@schleicher_failed

Unfortunately, the coalition supporting the dissolution of the Assembly does not constitute a majority. There will be elections as scheduled.

@reject
title: Reject Staal's schemes.
subtitle: The Assembly will continue to meet.
on-arrival: labor_dissent += 10 if works_program = 0

In the end, there is no uptake for Staal's schemes by any political party.